From befd2ba629fda14c50f88932dfb9f003aad7fd99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:52:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add SBA Lender Index page and link it from the home page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds /lenders — the top 100 SBA 7(a) lenders ranked by how much of
their book actually funds business acquisitions, rather than by raw
7(a) volume. The two are close to uncorrelated: Northeast Bank is 4th
nationally by dollars and does not list acquisition as a loan purpose.

Built on the existing design tokens, fonts, nav and footer, so it needs
no CSS changes to index.html. vercel.json already sets cleanUrls, so the
file serves at /lenders.

Home page: nav link, footer link, and a contextual link on the
"SBA financing opportunity -> Lender" row in the Graph section.

Scoring is commitment (acquisition share of book, 55 pts) plus depth
(absolute acquisition dollars, log-scaled, 45 pts). Every row exposes
its own arithmetic. Equity overlays, seller-note posture and
time-to-close are deliberately excluded from the score because no
lender publishes them; they appear as sourced notes instead.

Sourcing caveats are documented on the page: the public re-publishers
of the SBA FOIA change-of-ownership cut do not reconcile with each
other, so rank order is reliable but individual integers are not.
